@startuml transaction-status
' transactionStatus for a single SEPA credit transfer — SRC-IG §14.13 and §4.14.1.
' PROPOSAL generated by AI. Only the states this MVP can reach are drawn; the full code list is
' in the OpenAPI schema. Which end status the bank reports depends on DCP (Q-31).
title transactionStatus (SRC-IG §14.13) — INV-PAY-02

[*] --> RCVD : payment initiation received
RCVD --> RJCT : SCA window closed without a finalised authorisation (INV-PAY-03)
RCVD --> ACTC : authorised, technical and semantic validation passed
ACTC --> ACSP : accepted for execution by core banking
ACSP --> ACSC : settlement on the debtor account completed
ACTC --> RJCT : refused by core banking
ACSP --> RJCT : refused during execution
RJCT --> [*]
ACSC --> [*]

note right of ACTC
  Which of ACTC, ACCP, ACFC or ACSC the
  bank reports depends on whether DCP
  books in batch or in real time. Q-31, H-04.
end note

note bottom
  The flow diagrams of §5.1.8-§5.1.10 use ACCT and REJT.
  Neither is in the §14.13 code list. The code list wins:
  C-03, W-SPEC-01.
end note
@enduml
